      "parent_version": "0.2.1",
      "rationale": "pick_place@0.2.2 replaces the stock hold monitor with `SmoothedHoldMonitor`, which judges object-to-gripper drift on the mean of the last 8 raw observations (thresholds 4 cm sustained / 7 cm hard) instead of a single raw sample against 3 cm.\nIt targets the dominant gate failures (timeout \"still holding\" and grasp_slip, 24 of 27): every one of them had observation noise std near 1\u20131.5 cm, which makes a single sample's 3-D deviation routinely exceed 3 cm, so the monitor declared false slips mid-carry and the slip recovery opened the gripper and re-picked until the 300-step budget ran out.\nA temporary instrumented run confirmed the extra re-picks were not coming from the post-release placement check, leaving the slip detector as the trigger.\nReal drops (the cube falling 10 cm or more) still exceed the window-mean thresholds within a few steps, and the width-collapse check is unchanged.\nDev success went from 88% (35/40) to 98% (39/40), and 98/100 on 100 dev seeds; the remaining failures are grasp_slip on high-noise or high-yaw seeds.",
